5558
05:00:04,373 --> 05:00:05,063
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

5559
05:00:05,063 --> 05:00:09,856
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The E-Gates project is different from the Enhanced Border Control System

5560
05:00:09,856 --> 05:00:14,119
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: that is being proposed under the Public-Private Partnership arrangement.

5561
05:00:16,224 --> 05:00:18,541
Rep. Allan U. Ty: May we request everyone to please settle down?

5562
05:00:21,680 --> 05:00:23,378
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So can you make the distinction, Commissioner?

5563
05:00:23,803 --> 05:00:26,120
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, with the E-Gates project,

5564
05:00:26,120 --> 05:00:31,745
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: we aim to integrate that with the CAIS project.

5565
05:00:31,745 --> 05:00:34,398
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The CAIS project is a more holistic approach

5566
05:00:34,398 --> 05:00:36,803
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: because it does not only pertain to the E-Gates,

5567
05:00:37,051 --> 05:00:40,712
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: but also to our integration with the systems of Interpol,

5568
05:00:41,137 --> 05:00:43,542
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: as well as the Advanced Passenger Information System,

5569
05:00:44,002 --> 05:00:45,842
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: and biometrics.

5570
05:00:46,142 --> 05:00:51,926
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We also can log in to a billion facial images.

5571
05:00:52,634 --> 05:00:55,410
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And we also have, under the CAIS program,

5572
05:00:55,976 --> 05:01:02,362
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: the reactive screening based on facial contortions

5573
05:01:02,910 --> 05:01:06,023
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: or in reaction to certain forms of questioning.

5574
05:01:06,430 --> 05:01:09,348
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And we can also access open source intelligence.

5575
05:01:09,808 --> 05:01:13,841
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Not only can we access the 194 countries that are members of Interpol,

5576
05:01:13,876 --> 05:01:14,584
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: their databases,

5577
05:01:14,584 --> 05:01:16,176
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: we can access that.

5578
05:01:16,600 --> 05:01:19,006
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But also, we can access,

5579
05:01:19,165 --> 05:01:22,030
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: we can access any information from open sources,

5580
05:01:22,189 --> 05:01:23,197
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: meaning over the internet.

5581
05:01:24,206 --> 05:01:26,045
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Facebook, that can be accessed, Your Honor.

5582
05:01:26,841 --> 05:01:28,663
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So this is under the PPP program?

5583
05:01:28,840 --> 05:01:29,317
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

5584
05:01:29,583 --> 05:01:31,741
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Thank you, Commissioner Viado.

5585
05:01:31,917 --> 05:01:32,643
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Thank you, Your Honor.

5586
05:01:32,766 --> 05:01:34,606
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Let me go to LRA Administrator.

5587
05:01:36,649 --> 05:01:37,799
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Mr. Administrator,

5588
05:01:39,355 --> 05:01:41,920
Rep. Allan U. Ty: in your proposed 2027 budget,

5589
05:01:42,380 --> 05:01:43,211
Rep. Allan U. Ty: proposed budget,

5590
05:01:43,600 --> 05:01:46,678
Rep. Allan U. Ty: how much is under special account?

5591
05:01:46,678 --> 05:01:51,376
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: What budget?

5592
05:01:51,436 --> 05:02:01,810
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, it's $1.8 billion.

5593
05:02:03,329 --> 05:02:05,328
Rep. Allan U. Ty: $1.780 billion?

5594
05:02:05,328 --> 05:02:06,468
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Yes, Your Honor.

5595
05:02:06,468 --> 05:02:09,946
Rep. Allan U. Ty: What is the source of your special account in the general fund, Mr. Administrator?

5596
05:02:09,946 --> 05:02:14,543
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, the special account is Fund 151.

5597
05:02:14,543 --> 05:02:20,060
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: It is a special account provided by PD 1529,

5598
05:02:20,060 --> 05:02:26,836
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: where, from our collections, we are allowed to retain 20% of our earnings, Paul.

5599
05:02:26,836 --> 05:02:27,776
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor.

5600
05:02:28,116 --> 05:02:29,095
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Please settle down.

5601
05:02:32,503 --> 05:02:33,143
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Quiet, please.

5602
05:02:36,141 --> 05:02:38,480
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Where does the 80% of the collection go?

5603
05:02:38,700 --> 05:02:40,699
Rep. Allan U. Ty: How about the balance of 80%?

5604
05:02:40,819 --> 05:02:41,518
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Where does it go?

5605
05:02:41,518 --> 05:02:45,256
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, the 80% goes directly to the National Treasury,

5606
05:02:45,656 --> 05:02:52,392
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: and we retain 20% subject to the approval of the DBM on the releases of the 20%.

5607
05:02:52,392 --> 05:02:57,210
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So the 20% in the amount of 1.7,

5608
05:02:57,830 --> 05:03:00,308
Rep. Allan U. Ty: can we use that amount?

5609
05:03:00,308 --> 05:03:06,185
Rep. Allan U. Ty: To pay for titling of free patents issued by the DENR?

5610
05:03:06,185 --> 05:03:18,978
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, the 1.7 billion is 15% only out of the 20% it represents.

5611
05:03:18,978 --> 05:03:52,240
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, we believe that it can be used for it.

5612
05:03:52,240 --> 05:03:57,717
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: The coverage of the special account refers to MOOE accounts and capital outlay.

5613
05:03:58,436 --> 05:04:06,672
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Because, Administrator, there are thousands of unclaimed free patents before the Registry of Deeds all over the Philippines.

5614
05:04:06,672 --> 05:04:15,707
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So, probably, can you account for the free patents, unclaimed free patents, in all the Registry of Deeds all over the Philippines?

5615
05:04:15,707 --> 05:04:17,106
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Yes, Your Honor, you are correct.

5616
05:04:17,106 --> 05:04:21,724
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: We have made that observation in our visits to the different Registers of Deeds.

5617
05:04:21,724 --> 05:04:27,860
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: We have observed several, if not thousands, of unregistered patents previously.

5618
05:04:27,860 --> 05:04:38,615
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: This was covered by an agreement with the DENR, which paid for the registration of the patents.

5619
05:04:38,615 --> 05:04:42,612
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Subsequently, they removed that funding.

5620
05:04:42,612 --> 05:04:54,966
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: So, perhaps with the approval of the DBM, we can utilize it in registering some of these, or all the remaining patents issued.

5621
05:04:54,966 --> 05:04:57,684
Rep. Allan U. Ty: To be taken from the special account?

5622
05:04:57,844 --> 05:05:02,581
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Yes, Your Honor, if we can maximize the utilization to 20%.

5623
05:05:02,581 --> 05:05:03,661
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Thank you.

5624
05:05:03,661 --> 05:05:09,678
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So, on the other matter, Mr. Administrator, what is the legal responsibility of the

5625
05:05:09,678 --> 05:05:15,714
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Registry of Deeds and the LRA for the safekeeping maintenance of Certificate of Titles?

5626
05:05:15,714 --> 05:05:16,614
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Please, quiet down.

5627
05:05:16,614 --> 05:05:32,685
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honour, under PD 1529, the function of the main function of the Registers of Deeds is the main repository of all the

5628
05:05:32,725 --> 05:05:34,584
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: titles and supporting documents.

5629
05:05:34,844 --> 05:05:36,343
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So it's a registry of deeds?

5630
05:05:36,523 --> 05:05:37,063
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Yes, Your Honor.

5631
05:05:37,502 --> 05:05:44,639
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Is the registry of deeds required to prepare an inventory of titles which have been lost,

5632
05:05:44,958 --> 05:05:48,436
Rep. Allan U. Ty: destroyed, or rendered unusable by deterioration?

5633
05:05:48,436 --> 05:05:56,372
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, under PD 1529, the RDs are obliged to conduct an inventory annually.

5634
05:05:56,372 --> 05:06:03,748
Rep. Allan U. Ty: I would suppose that would also include all titles, whether it has been lost or damaged in their custody.

5635
05:06:05,227 --> 05:06:13,763
Rep. Allan U. Ty: In case of lost administrator of title, who has the legal responsibility for judicial reconstitution?

5636
05:06:14,322 --> 05:06:19,420
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, unfortunately, when the title is lost, the RD copy is lost.

5637
05:06:19,420 --> 05:06:25,176
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Under RA 26, as amended by RA 6732,

5638
05:06:25,176 --> 05:06:30,054
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: the responsibility is given to the owner of the title.

5639
05:06:30,633 --> 05:06:34,431
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: The responsibility was taken away from the RD.

5640
05:06:34,871 --> 05:06:39,609
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Previously, the RD was allowed to initiate reconstitution cases,

5641
05:06:39,828 --> 05:06:48,164
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: but because of the passage of the law and because of a Supreme Court decision involving the RD of Malabon or Mandaluyong,

5642
05:06:48,164 --> 05:06:54,161
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: the Supreme Court said that the RDs cannot undertake the filing.

5643
05:06:55,160 --> 05:06:56,319
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Under the reconstitution case.

5644
05:06:57,679 --> 05:07:03,376
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Sir Administrator, is there no exception to the rule under RA 6732?

5645
05:07:03,695 --> 05:07:08,553
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Under RA 26, as amended by RA 6732,

5646
05:07:09,772 --> 05:07:14,050
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: administrative reconstitution can be undertaken by the LRA

5647
05:07:14,330 --> 05:07:24,884
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: if the Administrator has evaluated that at least 10% of the titles in the RD has been lost,

5648
05:07:25,144 --> 05:07:29,741
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: But in no case should it be less than 500 titles.

5649
05:07:30,601 --> 05:07:40,895
Rep. Allan U. Ty: As you mentioned earlier, Mr. Administrator, you said the Registry of Deeds are required or mandated to have an inventory of lost titles.

5650
05:07:41,355 --> 05:07:46,652
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So based on the submission, did the Registry of Deeds make the submission?

5651
05:07:47,392 --> 05:07:51,030
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: They are required to conduct an inventory which should also include all lost titles.

5652
05:07:51,030 --> 05:07:59,805
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Some of the RDs have complied with the provisions of the law, and we are closely monitoring also the other RDs, Your Honor.

5653
05:08:00,245 --> 05:08:18,295
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Let's say in case the administrative threshold is not met, what can your office do to assist those lost titles, individual lost titles,

5654
05:08:18,295 --> 05:08:20,054
Rep. Allan U. Ty: considering that the loss?

5655
05:08:21,013 --> 05:08:25,671
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Loss was in the Registry of Deeds, am I not correct?

5656
05:08:26,390 --> 05:08:37,564
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, it is quite unfortunate that the burden is given to the registered owner in undertaking the registration or reconstitution of lost titles.

5657
05:08:37,964 --> 05:08:47,179
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: And on our part, what we can do is only provide them with the assistance of providing some of the necessary documents that they will need

5658
05:08:47,179 --> 05:08:50,977
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: in filing the appropriate constitution case with the courts, Your Honor.

5659
05:08:50,997 --> 05:08:52,996
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Let's go to Friar Lands.

5660
05:08:52,996 --> 05:09:03,990
Rep. Allan U. Ty: In case of loss of Friar Lands or has been lost or destroyed, and the DNR issued subsequent deed of conveyance,

5661
05:09:03,990 --> 05:09:10,986
Rep. Allan U. Ty: what will happen to the registration of the deed of conveyance before the Registry of Deeds?

5662
05:09:10,986 --> 05:09:12,985
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Thank you, Your Honor, for bringing it up.

5663
05:09:12,985 --> 05:09:16,983
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: We have several Friar Lands across the country.

5664
05:09:16,983 --> 05:09:17,982
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: We have the OCDC.

5665
05:09:20,961 --> 05:09:25,958
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: We have the OCDC, which is supposedly in the custody of the Registers of Deeds.

5666
05:09:25,958 --> 05:09:29,956
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: And the owner's copy is supposedly with the LMB.

5667
05:09:29,956 --> 05:09:41,949
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: It is unfortunate that some of the RDs have been destroyed or damaged, which included the titles also.

5668
05:09:41,949 --> 05:09:47,946
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: And it is also unfortunate that LMB has also been burned.

5669
05:09:47,946 --> 05:09:50,425
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Their head office in Binondo was burned.

5670
05:09:50,425 --> 05:09:55,422
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: So they have also lost some of the owner's copies of these titles.

5671
05:09:55,422 --> 05:10:03,417
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: But I would like to inform Your Honor that we are currently talking to the LMB,

5672
05:10:03,417 --> 05:10:08,415
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: since they have lifted the moratorium on the issuance of deeds of conveyance,

5673
05:10:08,415 --> 05:10:18,409
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: to explore administrative remedies so that we can also help the awardees or claimants of these Friar Lands.

5674
05:10:18,409 --> 05:10:19,409
Rep. Allan U. Ty: What administrative remedies?

5675
05:10:19,409 --> 05:10:23,407
Rep. Allan U. Ty: What administrative remedies you are referring to on the part of the DNR?

5676
05:10:23,407 --> 05:10:26,405
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: We will still be discussing with the LMB, Your Honor.

5677
05:10:26,405 --> 05:10:33,401
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: In fact, we were supposed to have a meeting last week, but because of the weather, it did not permit it.

5678
05:10:33,401 --> 05:10:35,400
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: But we will be meeting with them soon.

5679
05:10:35,400 --> 05:10:46,350
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Perhaps, Your Honor, also with your help, you can also talk to the LMB to meet with us soon on this matter.

5680
05:10:46,360 --> 05:10:52,230
Rep. Allan U. Ty: I think the DNR is scheduled.

5681
05:10:52,240 --> 05:10:56,150
Rep. Allan U. Ty: We will have a budget hearing on Wednesday.

5682
05:10:56,160 --> 05:11:02,870
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Maybe, Administrator, if you can commit to us that you can be present here on Wednesday in the afternoon.

5683
05:11:02,878 --> 05:11:04,628
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: I will come, Your Honor.

5684
05:11:04,638 --> 05:11:06,120
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Thank you, Mr. Administrator.

5685
05:11:15,000 --> 05:11:18,430
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Okay, I will have my third round.

5686
05:11:18,440 --> 05:11:22,230
Rep. Allan U. Ty: I defer to Kong Reni.

5687
05:11:22,240 --> 05:11:23,270
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Thank you, Your Honor.

5688
05:11:23,280 --> 05:11:24,430
Rep. Keith Micah "Atty. Mike" D.L. Tan: Thank you, Kong Alan.

5689
05:11:24,440 --> 05:11:30,270
Rep. Keith Micah "Atty. Mike" D.L. Tan: Next in line from the minority again, Rep. Renee Co.

5690
05:11:30,280 --> 05:11:31,670
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you very much, Chair.

5691
05:11:31,680 --> 05:11:35,390
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And thank you again for DOJ for continuing to be here.

5692
05:11:35,400 --> 05:11:45,750
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My next questions would be in relation to the supposed closure or nearing closure of the New Bilibid Prison.

5693
05:11:45,760 --> 05:11:53,390
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So it's been on the news that the Bureau of Corrections transferred 15,730 inmates ahead of the closure.

5694
05:11:53,400 --> 05:11:58,548
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Puwede pong matanong, since this is a huge endeavor,

5695
05:11:58,558 --> 05:12:02,990
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Logistically, ano pong budgetary provisions?

5696
05:12:03,000 --> 05:12:17,270
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Paano po napondohan ng DOJ 'yung pagpapalipat po ng mga inmates, mass transfer operation, transportation, security, etc. po?

5697
05:12:17,280 --> 05:12:26,350
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: With the permission of the Secretary, Mr. Chair, the transfer of the PDLs, ginagawa po 'yan yearly.

5698
05:12:26,360 --> 05:12:34,470
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: And it's with the support of the budget of Bucor using its MOE.

